ms in manageable steps through dialogue."}, "generative_agents_evaluators": {"answer": 100, "evidence_id": "ev-f03e4b7f1b7fc6e66886", "page": 47, "quote": "Whether the Generative Agents system generates believable behavior is evaluated with the help of 100 human evaluators. These were enlisted to rank believability of the communication patterns on four categories"}}, "outlook": {"agenda_topics": {"answer": ["training_data", "hallucination", "agent_behavior", "self_reflection", "safety"], "evidence_id": "ev-99f0f0a37d328bfed1a9", "page": 51, "quote": "Topic Challenge Training Data Finetune with inference time reasoning data Convergent/stable reinforcement learning VLA, Multimodal signals, such as speech Hallucination Use Self Verification Use Mechanistic Interpretability Use Open Ended/Open World Models for exploration Agent Behavior Scalable simulation infrastructure, role playing Distill reasoning to small models Models of agent and human behavior, emergent behavior, future of society Self reflection In-model self reflection and metareasoning Metacognition, personality Automated Scientific Discovery Safety Assistants: Responsibility, liability Privacy, fairness of data Wider application areas for assistants Table 4. Summary of Research Agenda for Agentic LLM"}, "shared_foundations": {"answer": ["reasoning", "self_verification"], "evidence_id": "ev-01ce8948bcc88d235ea3", "page": 52, "quote": "Robotic interaction and tool-use build on grounded retrieval augmentation, social interaction (such as theory of mind) builds on self reflection, and all categories benefit from reasoning and self-verification."}}}
